title: Ekla Chalo Re
artist: Rabindranath Tagore
origin: India
culture: Bengali
genre: World
language: bn
key: C major
tempo: 252
meter: 6/8
pickup: 4
intro: 2
outro: 1
style: indian
guide: flute
year: 1905
attribution: Words and music by Rabindranath Tagore, written in 1905 to a Baul-style tune (Tagore died in 1941), so both are public domain. This is the refrain ("If no one answers your call, walk alone"), from the staff notation in the Sangeet Natak Akademi anthology of Tagore songs. The flat 7th (B flat) on "ekla cholo" is expected to show as out-of-key.
source_url: https://bn.wikisource.org/wiki/%E0%A6%AA%E0%A6%BE%E0%A6%A4%E0%A6%BE:%E0%A6%B8%E0%A7%8D%E0%A6%AC%E0%A6%B0%E0%A6%B2%E0%A6%BF%E0%A6%AA%E0%A6%BF_-_Anthology_of_One_Hundred_Songs_of_Rabindranath_Tagore_in_Staff_Notation_(Volume_I).pdf/%E0%A7%A7%E0%A7%A6%E0%A7%AB
tags: bengali, tagore, rabindra sangeet, india, courage, walk alone
# Dadra (3+3). Written in 6/8 with the eighth note as the beat: the source's quarter note is one beat here.

